Article 4 Under any of the following circumstances, the discharge of pollutants shall not be deemed as direct discharge into the environment, and no environmental protection tax shall be paid for the corresponding pollutants:
(1) Where enterprises, public institutions, or other business operators discharge taxable pollutants to sewage centralized treatment facilities or domestic waste centralized treatment facilities established according to law;
(2) Where enterprises, public institutions, or other business operators store or dispose of solid wastes in facilities or sites that meet the environmental protection standards prescribed by the State or local authorities.

Article 7 The tax basis for taxable pollutants shall be determined in accordance with the following methods:
(1) For taxable air pollutants, it shall be determined by the number of pollution equivalents converted from the discharge amount of pollutants;
(2) For taxable water pollutants, it shall be determined by the number of pollution equivalents converted from the discharge amount of pollutants;
(3) For taxable solid wastes, it shall be determined by the discharge amount of solid wastes;
(4) For taxable noise, it shall be determined by the number of decibels exceeding the standards prescribed by the State.

Article 10 The discharge amount of taxable air pollutants, water pollutants, and solid wastes, as well as the decibel number of noise, shall be calculated in accordance with the following methods and order:
(1) For taxpayers that have installed and are using automatic pollutant monitoring equipment that meets the requirements prescribed by the State and monitoring specifications, the calculation shall be made based on the automatic monitoring data;
(2) For taxpayers that have not installed or used automatic pollutant monitoring equipment, the calculation shall be made based on monitoring data issued by monitoring agencies that meet the relevant requirements prescribed by the State and monitoring specifications;
(3) For those that are unable to meet monitoring conditions due to the large variety of pollutants discharged, the calculation shall be made based on the pollutant discharge coefficients and material balance calculation methods prescribed by the competent department of ecological environment of the State Council;
(4) For those that cannot calculate in accordance with the methods specified in items (1) to (3) of this Article, the calculation shall be verified and made based on the sampling estimation methods prescribed by the competent department of ecological environment of the people's government of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government.

Article 11 The payable amount of environmental protection tax shall be calculated in accordance with the following methods:
(1) The payable tax amount for taxable air pollutants shall be the number of pollution equivalents multiplied by the specific applicable tax amount;
(2) The payable tax amount for taxable water pollutants shall be the number of pollution equivalents multiplied by the specific applicable tax amount;
(3) The payable tax amount for taxable solid wastes shall be the discharge amount of solid wastes multiplied by the specific applicable tax amount;
(4) The payable tax amount for taxable noise shall be the specific applicable tax amount corresponding to the number of decibels exceeding the standards prescribed by the State.

Article 12 In the following circumstances, environmental protection tax shall be temporarily exempted:
(1) Where agricultural production (excluding large-scale breeding) discharges taxable pollutants;
(2) Where mobile pollution sources such as motor vehicles, railway locomotives, non-road mobile machinery, ships, and aircraft discharge taxable pollutants;
(3) Where urban or rural sewage centralized treatment facilities or domestic waste centralized treatment facilities established according to law discharge corresponding taxable pollutants without exceeding the discharge standards prescribed by the State or local authorities;
(4) Where taxpayers comprehensively utilize solid wastes that meet the environmental protection standards prescribed by the State or local authorities;
(5) Other circumstances approved by the State Council for tax exemption.
The tax exemption provisions in item (5) of the preceding paragraph shall be reported by the State Council to the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress for record.
